title: What a save reads there
pid: 38c15888-c19d-41ae-9e9e-b943fe847248
body: |2-
  The save's traversal (=visit_forks_folder= in
  =server/from_text/local_fieldintent_collection/traverse.rs=) reads
  the folder's claiming members as N's 'forks', and visits a claiming
  member as a forkee as such and one claiming nothing as a forker as
  such; neither is save-eligible, so neither's partial content is ever
  read as its whole list. It also emits a signal,
  =FieldIntent::ForksFolderMembers=, listing every vognode the folder
  shows, claiming or not, but those marked for deletion. Visibility
  resolution then hides in N each member of the folder as the view
  drew it ('forks_folder_members_shown' with N's forkees on disk; in the diff
  view, whose forks folders hold direct partners only, N's forkees and
  forker-only members) that would stand in it claiming nothing after
  the save (with N's forkees as the save leaves them), that the folder
  no longer shows, and that N does not hide already
  (=resolve_forks_folder_removals= in =resolve_visibility.rs=), before
  the edits of the hidden-outside folder, which run last. So a forkee
  whose deletion ends N's fork of it is hidden only where another
  mirror still joins it to N, and an indirect member only that forkee
  joined to N is not hidden. So:
  - typing a member there, claiming, makes N fork it;
  - deleting a forkee ends N's fork of it;
  - deleting a forker-only or an indirect member hides it in N, and
    it leaves the forks folder for the hidden-outside folder; removing
    it there unhides it, and it is drawn in the forks folder again;
  - deleting a mutual ends N's fork of it and hides it;
  - detaching a mutual ends N's fork of it only: it stands as a
    forker, claiming nothing;
  - attaching a forker-only member makes N fork it: a mutual;
    attaching an indirect member makes N fork it;
  - in a forkee as such E, drawn editable: E's title and body are saved
    when the user owns E, and refused (a text claim) when it is foreign;
    cutting one of E's children (one the view drew there, by the graph
    before the save, that the buffer shows neither under E nor in E's
    folder of what the user keeps elsewhere or of what N hides in it)
    hides it in N unless N, or a note the user owns
    but E, contains it after the save, and a child N hides,
    shown claiming under E, is unhidden (the forkee-visibility step), a
    save that would hide or unhide anything in a foreign N being
    refused; a child placed under E that E's list does not name (a
    headline typed there, or a node moved there) joins E's content,
    after the sibling it follows, when the user owns E, and is refused
    otherwise;
  - in a forker as such F, drawn editable: F's title and body are saved
    or refused as E's are, and a child placed under F joins F's
    content as under E; a child N hides, shown claiming under F, is
    unhidden; a child F showed that the buffer no longer shows under
    F, nor in F's folder of what the user keeps elsewhere or of what N
    hides in it, was cut from it (what F showed is read as its content less what
    N contains or hides and what the user kept elsewhere, wherever F is
    a mirror of N, 'is_mirror_of', an indirect member included), which
    makes N fork F (a mutual now, where F forks N) and hides the child
    in N unless N, or a note the user owns but F, contains it after the
    save (the
    forker-visibility step, 'resolve_forker_visibility'); the view
    the save redraws gives F's headline its claim, as every refresh
    gives each member of a forks folder the claim the graph gives it
    ('claim_forks_folder_members_as_the_graph_does'); under a
    foreign N such a save is refused, as under E; a cut from a mutual
    whose claim the same save removes only hides;
  - deleting a restricted viewnode (a member whose node the skgrepo
    restriction keeps out), from the forks folder or the hidden-outside
    folder, changes no relationship to the note it stands for: the
    save leaves the forks and hides involving it as they are, and the
    rerender draws it again ('preserve_invisible_members' in
    'supplement_from_disk.rs', and the two steps above).
  The hidden-outside folder holds N's hides that no member the forks
  folder shows contains, forkee, forker or indirect
  ('hidden_outside_of_fork_partners'); its edits are read against the
  same members ('apply_hiddenoutside_edits'), so a hide of what only a
  forker contains, unhidden under that forker as such, is not hidden
  again by a buffer that keeps the hidden-outside folder.
